<h1>Privacy: what we do not collect</h1>
<p class="emst-lede">The EMST explorer holds no personal data. It is a set of static pages; there is no server program behind it.</p>
<ul class="usa-list">
  <li><strong>No accounts, no sign-in, no cookies.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>No analytics, trackers or third-party content.</strong> Every font, stylesheet, image and script is served from this site. The page security policy forbids loading anything from elsewhere and forbids scripts from making any network connection.</li>
  <li><strong>Your gap-check answers never leave your device.</strong> They exist in the open page only. They are saved only if you choose "Save to file", and then only to your own downloads folder. Opening a saved file reads it in your browser; nothing is uploaded.</li>
  <li><strong>Nothing you type goes into the address bar.</strong> Links carry only role, competency and register identifiers.</li>
  <li><strong>Search runs in your browser.</strong> The search page loads its whole index with the page, before you type, so the site cannot see what you search for.</li>
  <li><strong>No browser storage.</strong> The explorer does not use local storage, session storage or IndexedDB.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What the host can see</h2>
<p>Like any website, the server that hosts these pages can log which pages are requested, by which network address, as part of ordinary web serving. The explorer cannot switch that off. If an agency mirrors the site on its own .gov host, that host's logging policy applies; the federal Digital Analytics Program, if added there, sees page views only.</p>
<h2>Team files</h2>
<p>If colleagues share their saved gap-check files with you for a team grid, those files are personal development records. Collect them only with each person's agreement, keep them in your organization's own systems and delete them when no longer needed. The team grid shows counts only, and only when at least 5 files are combined.</p>
<p>For development and planning only. EMST is not a selection instrument, not a classification basis and not for RIF, adverse action or performance-rating decisions.</p>
